const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"研究问题",en:"Research question"},body:{zh:"论文在识别的结构向量自回归框架中研究金融条件冲击和不确定性冲击如何互动并影响宏观结果。 阅读时应将其放回原始样本、时点和制度环境中理解，不能把问题本身当作跨市场结论。",en:"The article studies how financial-condition and uncertainty shocks interact and affect macroeconomic outcomes within an identified structural vector autoregression framework. Read it as a bounded question, not as a conclusion that automatically travels beyond its sample, dates, or institutional setting."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.euroecorev.2016.02.020",label:{zh:"European Economic Review · DOI record · 来源说明",en:"European Economic Review · DOI record · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"研究设计",en:"Research design"},body:{zh:"它以惩罚函数方法在SVAR中区分冲击，变量定义、识别限制、滞后结构、样本期和不确定性代理都会决定脉冲响应解释。 比较对象、观察窗口和对照关系共同构成研究合同；改变其中任一选择，可能改变所检验的命题。",en:"It distinguishes shocks using a penalty-function approach in an SVAR, so variable definitions, identification restrictions, lag structure, sample period, and uncertainty proxy determine the impulse-response interpretation. The comparison, observation window, and control relation are part of the research contract; changing one can change the proposition being tested."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.euroecorev.2016.02.020",label:{zh:"European Economic Review · DOI record · 来源说明",en:"European Economic Review · DOI record · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"数据与时点",en:"Data and timing"},body:{zh:"需要带日期的信用利差和不确定性指标、宏观序列、发布版本、变换、政策与危机背景、样本频率以及完整的识别和滞后设定。 字段定义、可得时点和样本筛选必须与原研究分开记录，不能因变量同名或使用最新修订值便视为可比。",en:"Inputs require dated credit-spread and uncertainty measures, macroeconomic series, release vintages, transformations, policy and crisis context, sample frequency, and the complete identification and lag specification. Keep fields, availability timing, and sample filters separate from the original study: a same-named variable or later-revised database is not automatically comparable."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.euroecorev.2016.02.020",label:{zh:"European Economic Review · DOI record · 来源说明",en:"European Economic Review · DOI record · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"如何理解结果",en:"How to read the result"},body:{zh:"来源在既定识别设计下报告历史中的不利影响，并强调不确定性与金融条件收紧的交互；它不直接观测冲击，也不提供当前衰退概率。 它只支持来源描述的经验或理论关系，不能把相关性、模型拟合或历史表现升级为因果、可执行性或未来保证。",en:"The source reports historically adverse effects under its identification design and highlights interaction between uncertainty and tighter financial conditions; it does not observe shocks directly or produce a current recession probability. This remains the empirical or theoretical relation described by the source; it does not turn association, fit, or historical performance into causality, an executable procedure, or a future guarantee."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.euroecorev.2016.02.020",label:{zh:"European Economic Review · DOI record · 来源说明",en:"European Economic Review · DOI record · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"复核清单",en:"Replication checks"},body:{zh:"保留数据版本和发布时滞；声明变换和单位；预定义识别及符号或惩罚限制；测试替代代理；报告置信区间；将危机叙事与模型输出分开。 开展后续分析前，应将这些选择写入版本化研究记录，并保留原始来源链接与访问日期。",en:"Preserve data vintages and release lags; state all transformations and units; predefine identification and sign or penalty restrictions; test alternative proxies; report confidence intervals; and separate crisis narratives from model output. Before extending the analysis, record these choices in a versioned note and retain the primary-source link and access date."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.euroecorev.2016.02.020",label:{zh:"European Economic Review · DOI record · 来源说明",en:"European Economic Review · DOI record · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"适用边界",en:"Scope boundary"},body:{zh:"该条导读引用 European Economic Review · DOI record。结构冲击估计依赖模型，不能在没有完整重复识别的情况下转成实时预测、政策建议或因果结论。 如需数值结论、参数、表格或稳健性检验，请回到原文并单独核对版本、附录与样本定义。",en:"This guide cites European Economic Review · DOI record. Structural-shock estimates are model-dependent and cannot be converted into a real-time forecast, policy recommendation, or causal conclusion without repeating the full identification exercise. For numerical conclusions, parameters, tables, or robustness tests, return to the original and separately verify the edition, appendices, and sample definitions."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.euroecorev.2016.02.020",label:{zh:"European Economic Review · DOI record · 来源说明",en:"European Economic Review · DOI record · source description"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"本文只整理“The Macroeconomic Impact of Financial and Uncertainty Shocks”公开说明的研究对象、设计与适用边界，不构成收益预测、交易规则或全文复现。结构冲击估计依赖模型，不能在没有完整重复识别的情况下转成实时预测、政策建议或因果结论。",en:"This guide only organizes the publicly described question and design of “The Macroeconomic Impact of Financial and Uncertainty Shocks”. It is not a return forecast, trading rule, or full-text replication. The source's stated scope remains controlling."}};export{e as default};
